  "question": {
    "text": "Which amongst the following is the strongest acid?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CH</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHI</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHBr</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Acidic character <math><mtext>&#945;</mtext></math> stability of conjugate base (anion)<br /><br />Stability of anion <math><mtext>&#945;</mtext><mo>-</mo><mi>M</mi></math> and <math><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>I</mi></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow><mo>-</mo> <mi>M</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mtext>dominance</mtext></mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> </math><br /><br />Electron withdrawing groups increase acidic strength. Among the given compounds, the electron withdrawing strength of substituents</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0333_c0ad12c9056a.png\" style=\"width: 349px; height: 107px;\" /></p><p>In case of halogen&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;order of halogen&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>Br</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></p><p>Hence, <math><mi>C</mi><mi>H</mi><mtext>&#160;</mtext><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> will be most acidic</p>"
